-- pending: SPEC §33 Open (a `for` over a call of a computation parameter: the loop's variables threaded through the argument)
-- A `for` over a call of a computation parameter (SPEC §33 *Open*): the `for`'s site threads the
-- loop's variables through the operation, so the argument, written at the call, would take them
-- with each element, at a type only `any` knows. Today the parameter's yields are handled by a
-- handler, `gen(()) |> any_true` (`corpus/effects-sum-gen.bc`).
--
-- Once it lands: `inr ()`, true; `live 0`.
--
-- now: 14:3: a `for` over a call of a computation parameter of `any`: not provided (its loop's variables would be threaded through the argument, SPEC §33 *Open*); handle the parameter's iteration effect with a handler, `f(()) |> h`
include yield
fn gen1() -> 1 with Yield[bool] = yield(false); yield(true)
fn any(gen: !(1 => 1 with Yield[bool])) -> bool =
  let mut r = false;
  for x in gen(()) { if x { r = true } else { () } };
  r
main -> bool = any(gen1)
